  "worked_solution": "Since the function $g(x)$ is continuous on $[2,4]$, the intermediate value theorem guarantees that $g(x)=k$ has a solution for each value of $k$ between $g(2)$ and $g(4).$\n\nSince $g(2)=0$ and $g(4)=-12,$ we must have \n$k\\in [-12,0].$\n\nAmong the given options, only $k=1$ does not belong to the interval $[-12,0].$",
